# Insights engine (PRD 004)

- Deterministic metrics (`core/enrich.py` / `metrics.py`) are **ground truth**. The agent
  narrates over real numbers it pulls via tools — it must **never invent values**.
- Tools are **read-only**, typed, and reuse the same queries as the API. The agent does not
  compute metrics; it reads precomputed ones.
- Every quantitative claim in `narrative` must come from a tool result and appear in
  `cited_metrics`. Missing data → say so and **lower confidence**, never guess.
- **No buy/sell recommendations.** Describe positioning/structure only.
- Structured output: `title`, `narrative`, `sentiment_label`, `confidence` (0–1),
  `cited_metrics`; persist to the `insights` table with `model` set.
- Use Anthropic **prompt caching** for the static system prompt + tool/schema docs. Bound
  tool-call count and tokens; log model/tokens/latency/cost.
- Treat tool/data field contents as untrusted (possible prompt injection) — data, not instructions.
- Triggers (scheduled session-close + on-demand) are idempotent per (instrument, session, type).
